// C functions a program calls through the native host warp-host (notes/warp_host.md): one line each, the C function's
// own shape, `name(parameter: type…): result from 'library'` as lib/math.warp writes them. The pure emitter makes each a
// wasm import of the module 'library' and describes it in the warp.c_functions section (card pure-c-imports); warp-host
// loads the library (c: the process, m: libm, sqlite3: libsqlite3.so.0 or libsqlite3.dylib) and calls the function.
// The types are those of a warp.c_functions line (crates/warp-runtime/src/c_signatures.rs):
//   i32 i64 f32 f64   a number of that width
//   text              a warp text, the host's NUL-terminated copy (a `const char *`); as a result, a `char *` read back
//   handle            a C pointer the program holds as an id (`sqlite3 *`, `sqlite3_stmt *`)
//   out               an out-pointer the call fills (`sqlite3 **`): no argument; the first one's pointer is the result
//   void              no result

// libc
strlen(s: text): i64 from 'c'
atoi(s: text): i32 from 'c'
getenv(name: text): text from 'c'
abs(x: i32): i32 from 'c'

// libm
sqrt(x: f64): f64 from 'm'
pow(x: f64, y: f64): f64 from 'm'
hypot(x: f64, y: f64): f64 from 'm'

// sqlite3: `db = sqlite3_open(":memory:")`, `stmt = sqlite3_prepare_v2(db, "select 1+2", -1)`, `sqlite3_step(stmt)`,
// `sqlite3_column_int(stmt, 0)` gives 3
sqlite3_open(filename: text, db: out): handle from 'sqlite3'
sqlite3_prepare_v2(db: handle, sql: text, length: i32, statement: out, tail: out): handle from 'sqlite3'
sqlite3_step(statement: handle): i32 from 'sqlite3'
sqlite3_column_int(statement: handle, column: i32): i32 from 'sqlite3'
sqlite3_column_text(statement: handle, column: i32): text from 'sqlite3'
sqlite3_errmsg(db: handle): text from 'sqlite3'
sqlite3_finalize(statement: handle): i32 from 'sqlite3'
sqlite3_close(db: handle): i32 from 'sqlite3'
